  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GFA Funding to BACKUP Health</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BACKUP&#x2019;s interventions supporting GF financing focus on three core areas of intervention, derived from the RSSH Modular Framework of the Global Fund (thereby feeding directly into the GF RSSH strategy):
(i)	Strengthening community engagement (e.g. new forms of participation in CCMs, Community-led Monitoring, effective linkages etc), with the aim to facilitate a shift from disease-specific community engagement towards systems thinking;
(ii)	Improving governance and coordination (e.g. new/improved oversight functions, methods for resource mapping and monitoring of GHI funding etc); 
(iii)	Providing people-centred health services (e.g. intersectoral planning; procedures for assessing and monitoring the integration of HTM services etc).</narrative>
  </description>
